NASTRAN-95-RUST
==============

A Rust rewrite of NASA's NASTRAN-95, developed module by module against a
reproducible Fortran baseline.

Source
------
Upstream:  https://github.com/nasa/NASTRAN-95
Pinned:    65e29e9db7b21a02bb42e723afa74fa7635ed765 (2015-12-03)
License:   NASA Open Source Agreement 1.3 (see vendor/nastran95/)

The vendor tree is pristine upstream source plus the deck corpus. The build
applies patches/nastran95.patch and strips DOS EOF bytes in a working copy;
it never edits the vendor tree.

Baseline
--------
scripts/build-baseline.sh builds build/nastran from the pinned source using
gfortran 12 in the pinned container (docker/Dockerfile). The build is the
oracle for Rust parity. The 1995 Sun f77 demoout files are a historical
sanity check, not a byte-exact target for a modern compiler.

Qualification (2026-11-26)
--------------------------
132 decks total:
  PASS       32  exact after stripping banners, dates, page headers
  KNOWN_DIFF 32  same structure; numeric within 1e-9 / 1e-3
  MISSING    11  needs RSCARDS/INP1/SOF artifacts not in the corpus
  RESTART     8  1995 output came from a checkpoint not in the corpus
  FAIL       49  residual structural or numeric differences

Qualified corpus: 64 decks (PASS + KNOWN_DIFF).
Report: qualification/report.json
Harness: parity/run_all.py, parity/classify.py, parity/qualify.py

Rust parity gate
----------------
A module ticket may merge only when:
  - the rebuilt baseline and the Rust build produce byte-identical normalized
    output for every deck that exercises the module, and
  - the reviewer has approved the diff and the parity report.

MISSING and RESTART decks are out of scope until their reference artifacts
are reconstructed. They must not be used to claim parity.

Layout
------
  vendor/nastran95/     pristine NASA source + inp/ + demoout/ + rf/ + alt/
  patches/              reviewed source patches for the modern build
  docker/               pinned toolchain image
  scripts/              build-baseline.sh, run-deck.sh
  parity/               run-all, normalize, diff, classify
  qualification/        report.json + SUMMARY
  inventory/            module list, call graph, leaf candidates
  crates/               Rust workspace (nastran-core, nastran-cli, fortran-bridge)

Build
-----
  docker build -t nastran-rs-build -f docker/Dockerfile .
  docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/work" nastran-rs-build scripts/build-baseline.sh
  docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/work" nastran-rs-build python3 parity/run_all.py
  docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/work" nastran-rs-build python3 parity/qualify.py
